From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rosemary port <port@local>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:05:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] osfmk/arm64: print the panic reason first, keep the stack walk in bounds

The RAM log from the last run came back with 1288 bytes and no panic text: the
hook dumped registers and started the stack walk before printing the reason,
and the walk ran off the top of the 16 KiB kernel stack, taking a second data
abort that killed the dump mid-line. Print the formatted reason first, then
registers, and bound the scan to the first 16 KiB boundary above sp.
---
diff --git a/osfmk/arm64/rosemary_early.c b/osfmk/arm64/rosemary_early.c
index 7dbbfc7..231c541 100644
--- a/osfmk/arm64/rosemary_early.c
+++ b/osfmk/arm64/rosemary_early.c
@@ -236,7 +236,17 @@ rosemary_early_diag(void)
 	diag_str(" sp=", &budget);
 	rosemary_early_hex64((uint64_t)sp, &budget);
 	diag_str("\n  stack:", &budget);
-	for (unsigned int i = 0; i < 2048; i++) {
+	/* Stay inside the current 16 KiB kernel stack: its top is the first
+	 * 16 KiB boundary above sp, and reading past it takes a second data
+	 * abort -- which is what truncated the previous dump at 1288 bytes. */
+	uintptr_t top = ((uintptr_t)sp | 0x3fffUL) + 1;
+	unsigned int nwords = (unsigned int)((top - (uintptr_t)sp) / 8) + 1;
+	if (nwords > 2048) {
+		nwords = 2048;
+	}
+	diag_str(" top=", &budget);
+	rosemary_early_hex64((uint64_t)top, &budget);
+	for (unsigned int i = 0; i < nwords; i++) {
 		uint64_t v = stk[i];
 		if (v >= 0xfffffe0007004000ULL && v < 0xfffffe0008108000ULL &&
 		    v != (i ? stk[i - 1] : 0)) {
@@ -260,8 +270,8 @@ rosemary_early_panic(const char *fmt, va_list *args)
 		return;
 	}
 	early_panicking = 1;
-	rosemary_early_diag();
-	/* not reached */
+	/* Reason first: the register dump and the stack walk below can fault on
+	 * their own, and the last run died before it ever printed this. */
 	rosemary_early_string("\nROSEMARY EARLY PANIC: ");
 	va_list copy;
 	va_copy(copy, *args);
@@ -269,6 +279,11 @@ rosemary_early_panic(const char *fmt, va_list *args)
 	va_end(copy);
 	rosemary_early_putc('\n');
 	__asm__ volatile("dsb sy" ::: "memory");
+	rosemary_early_diag();
+	/* not reached */
+	for (;;) {
+		__asm__ volatile("wfe");
+	}
 }
 
 void
